meta {
  name: Complete
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/google-calendar/complete/
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {"code": "{{google_oauth_code}}"}
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  Finishes the connection using the `code` the frontend received from the
  `/callback/` redirect. Exchanges the code with Google, fetches the
  connected account's own email, and saves the tokens onto whichever
  Associate's login email (Associate.user.email) matches it - not
  necessarily the signed-in caller. 400 "No Biopeak Nexus account uses this
  Google account's email..." if nobody's login email matches - staff must
  connect the same Google account they log into Biopeak Nexus with (a
  personal Gmail that differs from their login email won't resolve).

  Set env var google_oauth_code to the `code` value from the URL fragment
  (after the `#`) your browser lands on after approving consent (see
  Connect.bru's docs for the full manual flow) - paste it there, not
  directly into this body, so this request stays runnable straight from the
  collection.

  Method: POST
  Path: /google-calendar/complete/
  Source: integrations.google_calendar.views.GoogleCalendarCompleteView
  Auth: None — authentication_classes = [] (this view never reads
  request.user; the email match is what decides whose tokens actually get
  saved). The `auth: bearer` on this request is harmless but unnecessary.

  Success: {"detail": "Google Calendar connected.", "data": {"email": "...", "associate_id": "..."}}
}
